// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'id'
//
// `generationNode: { (nodeId)? generationElement }` is an ORDERED rule: the optional id
// comes FIRST. Writing it after the element -- which reads perfectly well and is how every
// other body in these grammars would take it -- is a parse error.
//
// Nearly every element body in Legend is an unordered `( ... )*` whose constraints are
// applied later by the walker. This is one of the few that is not, so a rewrite that applies
// the house style uniformly accepts this file, and a rewrite that hardcodes order elsewhere
// rejects files legend-engine accepts. Paired with neg-generation-node-missing-element.pure,
// which pins the same rule's other half.
###GenerationSpecification
GenerationSpecification fixture::neg::NodeIdAfterElement
{
   generationNodes: [
      {
         generationElement: fixture::neg::AvroConfig;
         id: 'afterTheElement';
      }
   ];
}
